config HANGAR_SYNC
	bool "Hangar: locks shared between environments"
	depends on FILE_LOCKING
	help
	  Locks taken with flock(2) or fcntl(2) on files under paths Hangar's
	  guest agent registers are taken for the environment as a whole from
	  the agent, through /dev/hangar-sync, before the local lock, and given
	  back when no process here holds one. Without the agent, locks are
	  local only.
